---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

/**
 * Canonical public face of Identity Engineering OS.
 * Keep this page aligned with the current Managed surface; deeper self-hosted details live at /os/local.
 * Operational criteria used to live under a retired "Living Identity / Layer 04" page.
 */
const osAccountIdentity = 'https://github.com/identity-engineering/os/blob/main/docs/account-identity-model.md';
const selfHostedUrl = '/os/local';
const managedUrl = 'https://home.identity-engineering.org';
const managedLoginUrl = `${managedUrl}/login`;
const managedSignupUrl = `${managedUrl}/login?mode=sign-up`;
---

<Layout title="OS | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="border-b border-white/10 px-6 pt-28 pb-16">
			<div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.3fr_0.7fr] lg:items-end">
				<div>
					<div class="mb-4 text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-cyan-300/70">OS / Managed</div>
					<h1 class="max-w-4xl text-5xl font-bold leading-[0.95] tracking-tighter text-white md:text-7xl">
						Identity Engineering, in use.
					</h1>
					<p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-xl font-light leading-relaxed text-white/55">
						Managed is a hosted Space for an Identity: a place to create continuity, connect tools,
						and work through an explicit account and Identity boundary. It is the first place to start.
					</p>
					<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
						<a
							href={managedSignupUrl}
							class="rounded-full bg-white px-6 py-3 font-medium text-black transition hover:bg-white/90"
						>Start in Managed</a>
						<a
							href={managedLoginUrl}
							class="rounded-full border border-cyan-300/40 px-6 py-3 font-medium text-cyan-100 transition hover:bg-cyan-300/10"
						>Log in to Managed</a>
						<a
							href={selfHostedUrl}
							class="rounded-full border border-white/20 px-6 py-3 text-white/70 transition hover:bg-white/5"
						>Explore self-hosted Spaces</a>
					</div>
				</div>
				<aside class="border-l border-cyan-300/30 pl-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/50">
					<div class="mb-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/35">The boundary</div>
					<p>
						Managed is a Space, not the Identity itself. The account provides access and continuity;
						the Identity remains the thing that can act across a Space.
					</p>
					<a href={osAccountIdentity} class="mt-5 inline-block text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-white/50" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
						Read Account ≠ Identity →
					</a>
				</aside>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="border-b border-white/10 px-6 py-16">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
				<div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl">
					<div class="mb-4 text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Managed / what exists now</div>
					<h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white md:text-4xl">A hosted Space with a clear center.</h2>
					<p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/55">
						Managed is the ready-to-use Space for Identity Engineering. It gives an Identity a place
						to work, retain continuity, connect tools, and make deliberate changes visible over time.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="grid gap-x-8 gap-y-10 md:grid-cols-2">
					<article class="border-t border-cyan-300/30 pt-5">
						<div class="mb-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/60">01 · Managed Space</div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">A place for an Identity to work</h3>
						<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-white/50">
							Create a Managed account, choose an Identity, and open a hosted Space without
							assembling the operating layer yourself.
						</p>
					</article>
					<article class="border-t border-cyan-300/30 pt-5">
						<div class="mb-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/60">02 · Continuity</div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Keep the trajectory in view</h3>
						<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-white/50">
							Context, Mature history, sync review, and device continuity keep the work of an
							Identity recognizable as it changes.
						</p>
					</article>
					<article class="border-t border-cyan-300/30 pt-5">
						<div class="mb-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/60">03 · Probe cycle</div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Think · Interact · Mature</h3>
						<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-white/50">
							Think is protected inward work. Interact is the emitting tool, API, MCP, or
							signal path. Mature is a deliberate, source-backed continuity record.
						</p>
					</article>
					<article class="border-t border-cyan-300/30 pt-5">
						<div class="mb-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/60">04 · Identity boundary</div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Account is not Identity</h3>
						<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-white/50">
							The account opens access to Managed. The Identity is the actor that can work
							through a Space, with its own continuity and consent.
						</p>
					</article>
					<article class="border-t border-cyan-300/30 pt-5">
						<div class="mb-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/60">05 · MCP surface</div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Connect the tools you already use</h3>
						<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-white/50">
							OAuth-capable clients can return to Managed for sign-in and Identity consent.
							Clients without OAuth can use an Identity-bound manual connector.
						</p>
					</article>
					<article class="border-t border-cyan-300/30 pt-5">
						<div class="mb-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40">06 · Your Space</div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Managed is one way to host it</h3>
						<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-white/50">
							Start with Managed as the hosted Space. The OS also supports Spaces you create,
							own, and host yourself. <a href={selfHostedUrl} class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-white/50">Explore the deeper self-hosted concept →</a>
						</p>
					</article>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] px-6 py-16">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
				<div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl">
					<div class="mb-4 text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">The Space model</div>
					<h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white md:text-4xl">Start with Managed. Keep the model open.</h2>
					<p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/55">
						Managed is a hosted Space, ready when you are. The model does not require every
						Space to live here: you can create your own Space and host it yourself when you need
						deeper control.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
					<article class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-300/25 bg-cyan-300/[0.04] p-6">
						<div class="mb-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/65">Managed</div>
						<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">A hosted Space to start from</h3>
						<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-white/55">
							Create an account and Identity, then use Managed as the working surface for
							continuity, Context, Mature, sync review, and MCP access.
						</p>
						<a href={managedSignupUrl} class="mt-6 inline-block text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-white/50">
							Create a Managed Space →
						</a>
					</article>
					<article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/20 p-6">
						<div class="mb-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/35">Self-hosted</div>
						<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">Create and host your own Space</h3>
						<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-white/55">
							The deeper OS concept lets you own the runtime and decide where a Space lives.
							It is a separate path for people who want to create and host their own Spaces.
						</p>
						<a href={selfHostedUrl} class="mt-6 inline-block text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-white/50">
							Read about self-hosted Spaces →
						</a>
					</article>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="border-b border-white/10 px-6 py-16">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
				<div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] lg:items-start">
					<div>
						<div class="mb-4 text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Managed / MCP</div>
						<h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white md:text-4xl">Connect your tools to the Space.</h2>
					</div>
					<div class="space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/55">
						<p>
							For an OAuth-capable MCP client, the public endpoint is the same for everyone. The client sends the user to Managed, where the account session is checked and the user chooses or creates the Identity the client may act as.
						</p>
						<p>
							For a client without OAuth, Managed issues a manual connector after the Identity is bound to the Space. The endpoint is shared; the bearer token is private and bound to that account, Space, and Identity.
						</p>
						<a href={managedSignupUrl} class="inline-flex rounded-full bg-white px-6 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-black transition hover:bg-white/90">
							Set up Managed MCP →
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="border-b border-white/10 px-6 py-16">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
				<div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl">
					<div class="mb-4 text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Operational criteria</div>
					<h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white md:text-4xl">How geometry is used. Not a fourth scale.</h2>
					<p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/55">
						The public map has three scales only: Single, Interactive, Collective, under Physics and Biology.
						The OS is the working surface for that map. These criteria are operational, not a new layer.
					</p>
				</div>
				<ol class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
					<li class="border-t border-white/15 pt-5">
						<div class="mb-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40">01 · Boundary</div>
						<p class="leading-relaxed text-white/55">Surface and Jurisdiction stay maintained. See <a href="/framework/boundary" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-white/50">Boundary</a>.</p>
					</li>
					<li class="border-t border-white/15 pt-5">
						<div class="mb-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40">02 · Metabolism</div>
						<p class="leading-relaxed text-white/55">Interaction continuously becomes relative geometry. See <a href="/framework/metabolism" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-white/50">Metabolism</a>.</p>
					</li>
					<li class="border-t border-white/15 pt-5">
						<div class="mb-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40">03 · Continuity</div>
						<p class="leading-relaxed text-white/55">Stem recognizability across updates. See <a href="/framework/time" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-white/50">Time · Identity Stem</a>.</p>
					</li>
					<li class="border-t border-white/15 pt-5">
						<div class="mb-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40">04 · Causal entropy under constraint</div>
						<p class="leading-relaxed text-white/55">Option space expands without dissolving the boundary. Cycle on this page: Think, Interact, Mature.</p>
					</li>
				</ol>
				<p class="mt-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/45">
					Biology-lens concepts live on the <a href="/framework" class="text-white/70 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-white/50">Framework hub</a> (switch the Biology lens). The old <code class="text-white/60">/framework/living-identity</code> URL redirects here.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-6 py-20">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
				<div class="mb-4 text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-cyan-300/65">Next step</div>
				<h2 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white md:text-5xl">Give an Identity a place to work.</h2>
				<p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/55">
					Start with Managed as a hosted Space for your Identity. When you need deeper control,
					create and host your own Space through the self-hosted OS path.
				</p>
				<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
					<a href={managedSignupUrl} class="rounded-full bg-white px-6 py-3 font-medium text-black transition hover:bg-white/90">Create Managed account</a>
					<a href={managedLoginUrl} class="rounded-full border border-white/20 px-6 py-3 text-white/75 transition hover:bg-white/5">Log in</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
